="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: TECH SOURCE FROM BOHOL" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/SimplyJun/~3/476610191/7-best-freeopen-source-image-viewers.html"&gt;7 Best Free/Open-source Image Viewers for Linux&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; By noreply@blogger.com (jun auza) on free/open-source &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Processing 1.0</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/processing-10/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/processing-10/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 3 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 20 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Woooo, right up my street &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://hackaday.com/2008/11/25/processing-10/"&gt;Processing 1.0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="snap_preview"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-6276" src="http://hackadaycom.files.wordpress.com/2008/11/2955430710_34b84eb301.jpg?w=450&amp;amp;h=450" alt="" height="450" width="450" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.processing.org/"&gt;Processing&lt;/a&gt;, the open source programming language designed for artists and other creative types, finally went 1.0. Processing inspired numerous outpourings of creativity and beauty, from &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://bricktable.wordpress.com/about/what-is-roots/"&gt;interactive art installations&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://hackaday.com/2008/11/22/advanced-beauty-generative-video-art/"&gt;sound sculptures&lt;/a&gt;. Improvements to Processing include OpenGL anti-aliasing, an extensible Tools menu, and the XML library included by default. You can read up on the &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://processing.org/reference/changes.html"&gt;changes&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.processing.org/download/index.html"&gt;download Processing&lt;/a&gt; and start playing with it yourself.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Spreadsheet Art</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/spreadsheet-art/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 08:36:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/spreadsheet-art/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is a time-lapse video of three &lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2008/08/man_proposes_using_google_eart.php" target="Bwindow"&gt;Google employees&lt;/a&gt; creating an 18,600 cell mosaic in a spreadsheet. As you will see, it has a nice&lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2007/12/man_plays_jingle_bells_on_grap.php" target="Bwindow"&gt; wintry theme&lt;/a&gt;. Namely, snowflakes.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/KpcgRlXe40k&amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;hl=en&amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/KpcgRlXe40k&amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;hl=en&amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true" width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Hybrid 3d rendering on GPU</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/hybrid-3d-rendering-on-gpu/</link><pubDate>Mon, 24 Nov 2008 12:10:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/hybrid-3d-rendering-on-gpu/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 5 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Hot hot hot&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip;.sweet eye candy.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base11195221"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table11195221" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://theamusementmachine.blogspot.com/"&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Amusement Machine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/ta